  "task_id": "tmm_optimize_a_29_layer_planar_multilayer_stack_on_a_20ffcb96fb",
  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 29-layer planar multilayer stack on a Fused Silica (SiO2 (Lemarchand)) substrate with Air incident medium. Materials are Ta2O5 (Gao) (High index) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) (Low index). Stack sequence: Alternating Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand), starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) at the air interface, ending with Ta2O5 (Gao) at the substrate interface. Layer 15 (central Ta2O5 (Gao)) is the defect layer. Design variables: Physical thickness of all 29 layers. Initialization: All layers initialized to quarter-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm, except Layer 15 which is initialized uniformly random between 375 nm and 385 nm. Optimizer: Gradient-based thickness optimization with cosine-annealing learning rate scheduler capped at 5e-4. Regularization: Add a penalty term to the loss function proportional to the sum of max(0, |thickness_i - thickness_{i+1}| - 60 nm) for all adjacent pairs. Objectives: Maximize mean transmittance at 1550 nm (single wavelength), minimize mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm band, minimize mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm band. Constraint: Total layers = 29. Materials resolved by name: Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize physical thicknesses of a 29-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric cavity on fused silica, maximizing mean transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in the 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands.",
